  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="bc4ffc02-f3ee-5a6a-bbf6-c89d910bab0d" activityNameId="7bff8751-baf9-5960-8235-a52437781c46" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Pipeline, natural gas, long distance, high capacity, onshore</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Pipeline, natural gas, long distance, high capacity, onshore
It is assumed that half of the pipelines are disposed in a discharge at the end of life, the other half stays in the soil. The life time of the pipeline is 40 years.;
UUID: ad3bef52-f8d7-3702-9d95-261dbcada713
This dataset describes the infrastructure needed for a long-distance pipeline onshore with a capacity from average 1.1e6 Sm3/h gas including material requirements, construction and disposal. Helicopter flights for inspection are included.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: The steel quantities are calculated on the basis of the geometry of the pipeline (diameter 1219mm, thickness 12.3 mm). Coating is assumed to be the same as in the low capacity onshore pipeline.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: environmental report 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_ad3bef52-f8d7-3702-9d95-261dbcada713.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="f4808887-5a57-5892-975e-ba0565a93e23" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
